content_data:
Use this endpoint to view statistics of event data over a period of time. Statistics returned include the number of attributed events (the number of events attributed to your ads), the number of preview events (the number of events generated by the ad preview), and the total number of events received from all data sources.

> <span style="color:DarkRed">**Important**</span><br>
> By using Events API endpoints, you agree to the [TikTok Business Products (Data) Terms](https://ads.tiktok.com/i18n/official/policy/business-products-terms) and that you will not share sensitive data with TikTok.

## Comparing v1.2 and v1.3 
 The following table outlines the differences between v1.2 and v1.3 endpoints. 
 ```xtable
|Changes{30%}|v1.2{35%}|v1.3{35%}|
|---|---|---|
|Endpoint path| /v1.2/pixel/event/stats/| /v1.3/pixel/event/stats/|
|Request parameter data type|`advertiser_id`: number <br>`pixel_ids`: number[] |`advertiser_id`: string<br> `pixel_ids`: string[] |
|Response parameter data type|`pixel_id`: number |`pixel_id`: string |
|New response parameters | / |`custom_event_type`<br>`browser_event_total_count`<br> `server_event_total_count` |
```

## Request

**Endpoint** https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3/pixel/event/stats/

**Method** GET

**Header**
```xtable
|Field{30%}|Data Type{15%}|Description{55%}|
|---|---|---|
|Access-Token {Required}|string|Authorized access token. For details, see [Authentication](https://ads.tiktok.com/marketing_api/docs?id=1738373164380162). |
```

**Parameters**
```xtable
|Field{30%}|Data Type{15%}|Description{55%}|
|---|---|---|
|advertiser_id {Required}|string| Advertiser ID. |
|date_range {Required}|object| Time range, which cannot exceed 30 days.<br><br><p><span style="color:darkred"><b>Note</b></span>: There may be slight differences between the event statistics obtained from this endpoint and the statistics displayed on [Events Manager](https://ads.tiktok.com/help/article/about-tiktok-events-manager). This is because the event statistics from this endpoint are based on UTC time, while the statistics displayed on Events Manager are based on the advertiser's time zone.|
#|start_date {Required}|string| Start time (UTC time). <br><br>Example:`"2020-02-16"`.|
#|end_date {Required}|string| End time (UTC time).<br><br> Example:`"2020-02-17"`. |
|pixel_ids {Required}|string[]| Pixel ID list.  <br><br>Max size: 10.|
```

